# The patched RTX 40 kernels (sm86/build.py --arch sm_89) that have run on an RTX 40 card, one line each:
#   <nvcc version> <hash> <what ran it>
# build.py writes qc_sm89_cubin.h only when what it built is listed here for the nvcc that built it, so a toolkit
# that compiles the kernel another way ships no patched kernel and the core runs the compiled one. The hash covers
# every section of the cubin but the names, so one line serves Linux and Windows builds (qc_sm86.ref says more).
# A line is added only after its file has run verify-core.js (all five checks) on an RTX 40 card through
# QUANTUS_CUDA_CUBIN_FILE, and the core's own startup check has passed there.

# QC_RED 3 with QC_KZ 1 and QC_DPRIME (goal/q3-rtx40 02b957a5, 20 Nov), 158 tails; no longer built (QC_DM_T0 from
# q3-rtx30 8ea9c793 adds 18 more). RTX 4070 Ti (Salad llmjob2 PC 23b4f1c3): startup check passed, verify-core all
# five PASS (542.29 MH/s, the compiled kernel 527.38 on the same PC); qcbench 539.11 / 538.43 against 525.58 / 523.12.
